# Atlas — expense claims + the unified approval inbox (Sprint 08)
# Login first (see auth.http) and paste the bearer token below.
# You also need a worker id — hire one via workers.http and paste it in.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE
@workerId = PASTE_WORKER_ID

### Submit an expense claim for a worker (HR/admin on behalf, v1) → 201
# Amount is a Money DTO: a decimal + its currency, always together (S07). Receipt is METADATA
# only — a url + filename; Atlas stores no binary this sprint.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workerId": "{{workerId}}",
  "amount": { "amount": 240.00, "currency": "USD" },
  "category": "Travel",
  "receiptUrl": "https://receipts.example/abc",
  "receiptFilename": "taxi.pdf",
  "note": "Client visit"
}

### Unknown category → 400 (a malformed request, not a business-rule violation)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workerId": "{{workerId}}",
  "amount": { "amount": 50.00, "currency": "USD" },
  "category": "Sorcery"
}

### Non-positive amount → 422 (a domain rule)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workerId": "{{workerId}}",
  "amount": { "amount": 0, "currency": "USD" },
  "category": "Meals"
}

### Approve a submitted claim → 200
POST {{host}}/api/v1/expenses/PASTE_CLAIM_ID/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deny a submitted claim, with an optional reason → 200
POST {{host}}/api/v1/expenses/PASTE_CLAIM_ID/deny
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Missing itemised receipt."
}

### Cancel a submitted or approved claim → 200 (a reimbursed claim cannot be cancelled)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/expenses/PASTE_CLAIM_ID/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one claim
GET {{host}}/api/v1/expenses/PASTE_CLAIM_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List the org's expense claims (org-scoped, cursor pagination as everywhere)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/expenses?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### THE PAYOFF: the unified approval inbox — pending LEAVE and EXPENSES in one worklist
# Submit a leave request (leave.http) AND an expense above, then call this: both appear, newest
# submitted first. `kind` tells the client which resource to POST the decision to.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/approvals?limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
